<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the May 23-26 Memorial Day weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. on Monday. Final data will be issued on Tuesday.</p>
<p> 1 (*) The Lost World: Jurassic Park ........... $90.1 million</p>
<p> 2 (*) Addicted To Love ........................ $12.1 million</p>
<p> 3 (1) The Fifth Element .......................  $8.2 million</p>
<p> 4 (4) Austin Powers ...........................  $5.8 million</p>
<p> 5 (3) Breakdown ...............................  $5.7 million</p>
<p> 6 (2) Fathers' Day ............................  $5.0 million</p>
<p> 7 (6) Liar Liar ...............................  $3.1 million</p>
<p> 8 (7) Night Falls On Manhattan ................  $2.3 million</p>
<p> 9 (5) Volcano .................................  $2.0 million</p>
<p>10(10) Anaconda ................................  $1.7 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parentheses, and * stands for new release. Including Thursday night previews, the total for &quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; was $92.7 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; and &quot;Liar Liar&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd. .</p>
<p>&quot;Addicted To Love&quot; and &quot;Fathers' Day&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The Fifth Element&quot; and &quot;Anaconda&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; and &quot;Night Falls on Manhattan&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
